<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Emmanuel IV of Sardinia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1751–<a href="/years/1819">1819</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Emmanuel IV was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and Duke of Savoy from 1796 to 1802. In December 1798 French troops occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a> and forced him to give up his mainland states, and he withdrew to the island of Sardinia. Grieving after the death of his wife, Clotilde of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, he abdicated in 1802 in favour of his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-i-of-sardinia">Victor Emmanuel I</a> and spent his last years in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, joining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-emmanuel-iv-of-sardinia.jpg" alt="Charles Emmanuel IV of Sardinia" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Giovanni Panealbo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Attributed_to_Panealbo_-_Charles_Emmanuel_IV_-_Venaria_Reale.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
